  "_why": "The top of the demand curve was 34/100 task-mapped, because the `declared` pass reads only the author's npm KEYWORDS and the most-installed servers declare none. @modelcontextprotocol/server-postgres says 'MCP server for interacting with PostgreSQL databases' in prose and carried no tag at all. Graded in session against web/data/tasks.json, from each capability's own published description.",
  "_rule": "Tag only what the author's own words support. Where the description is marketing, a badge dump, or a product with no honest home in a 69-task taxonomy of WORK (payments, fitness, train tickets, recipes), it is left untagged — a wrong shelf is worse than an empty one, and this taxonomy describes jobs people do, not every category of software.",

